WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.630
Love to laugh?

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.970
You're in luck, because some of the best comedies
ever made are getting sequels — and they're

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.364
coming sooner than you think…

00:00:08.364 --> 00:00:12.950
"We got one!"

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.760
A third sequel to Ghostbusters was on the
table for decades, and while Dan Aykroyd certainly

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.590
had ambitious plans for the franchise, they
sadly never panned out.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.280
Instead, fans got a reboot with Paul Feig's
2016 Ghostbusters, which featured a whole

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.443
new set of Ghostbusters played by Kristen
Wiig, Kate McKinnon, Leslie Jones, and Melissa McCarthy.

00:00:31.443 --> 00:00:36.370
That film's middling box office returns and
so-so critical reviews ensured that it would

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.290
never receive any sequels.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:43.750
And so Sony rebooted Ghostbusters once more
with 2021's Ghostbusters: Afterlife.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.890
Set in the world of the original Ghostbusters
films and featuring cameos from both living

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.989
and not-so-living members of the original
team, the film was a hit at the relatively

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:56.390
subdued COVID-era box office, prompting Sony
to greenlight a sequel.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:00.870
Jason Reitman, director of Ghostbusters: Afterlife
and son of original Ghostbusters director

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.990
Ivan Reitman, will return to co-write and
produce an Afterlife sequel, which is reportedly

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.020
titled Ghostbusters: Firehouse.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.610
Co-writing duties also go to Monster House's
Gil Kenan.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.890
As the end sequence of Afterlife suggests,
the film will take place in New York City,

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.180
just like the '80s Ghostbusters films.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.580
While a few cast members will be returning
from Afterlife, it hasn't yet been confirmed

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.750
whether Bill Murray, Dan Aykroyd, Ernie Hudson,
or Rick Moranis might return — but fans

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.193
are no doubt hoping for the best.

00:01:30.193 --> 00:01:34.750
Based on a series of sketches from Nickelodeon's
All That, Kenan and Kel's Good Burger hit

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:35.909
movie theaters in 1997.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:41.280
"Welcome to Good Burger, home of the Good
Burger, can I take your order?"

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.310
The Good Burger movie, which revolves around
a rivalry between the Good Burger fast food

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:50.740
joint and a soulless corporate chain, earned
a modest $23 million at the box office, but

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.560
nostalgia, home video, frequent airings on
TV, and Kenan Thompson's rise as an iconic

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.170
pop culture figure have turned the film into
a cult classic.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:04.750
Paramount took note of this and put in an
order for some more Good Burger in March 2023.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:10.270
Set to debut on Paramount+ sometime in 2023,
Good Burger 2 will follow a down-and-out Dexter

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:15.877
as he returns to Good Burger to work alongside
Ed, who's still employed at the restaurant decades later.

00:02:15.877 --> 00:02:20.819
Along with Thompson and Mitchell, Carmen Electra
will return as the would-be secret sauce recipe

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:22.220
thief Roxanne.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.869
Will the movie enjoy the cult following of
the original?

00:02:24.869 --> 00:02:26.700
Your guess is as good as ours.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.250
But here's hoping Good Burger 2 makes for
good eating either way.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:37.130
In 2002, My Big Fat Greek Wedding became a
pop culture phenomenon as huge as it was unexpected.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:43.849
The story originally began as a semi-autobiographical
one-woman show written and performed by Nia Vardalos.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:48.744
Actor and producer Rita Wilson saw it and
loved it, and soon enough, so did her husband, Tom Hanks.

00:02:48.744 --> 00:02:54.260
A few years later, they co-produced the film
adaptation, a blockbuster that grossed $368

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:59.629
million worldwide, making it the highest-earning
romantic comedy of all time.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:04.140
My Big Fat Greek Wedding led to a follow-up
movie, My Big Fat Greek Wedding 2, as well

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.090
as a spin-off on CBS.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:11.409
In June 2022, Vardalos announced in an Instagram
video the third movie had already begun filming

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:14.560
on location in Greece; filming wrapped two
months later.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.113
Vardalos directs the movie and reprises the
leading role of Toula at the same time.

00:03:19.113 --> 00:03:24.040
According to Us Weekly, a host of original
cast members will also return, including John

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:29.069
Corbett, Elena Kampouris, Andrea Martin, Louis
Mandylor, and Maria Vacratsis.

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:33.250
According to the movie's trailer, the sequel
finds the Portokalos family visiting Greece,

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:37.610
fulfilling a dying wish of patriarch Gus,
who wanted his descendants to experience the

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.259
village in which he was raised.

00:03:39.259 --> 00:03:44.669
My Big Fat Greek Wedding 3 is due for release
on September 8th, 2023.

00:03:44.669 --> 00:03:49.220
Considering the pile of films from the '80s
and '90s being reimagined for modern audiences,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.819
it was always going to be a matter of time
before the bizarre 1988 Tim Burton haunted

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:57.810
house comedy Beetlejuice got the sequel treatment.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.005
Sure enough, Beetlejuice 2 is finally in the
works.

00:04:01.005 --> 00:04:02.550
"It's showtime."

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:07.650
Warner Bros. confirmed that development on
the movie had begun at CinemaCon 2023.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:11.849
Soon after, it was announced that Wednesday's
Jenna Ortega had joined the cast, reportedly

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:15.010
playing the daughter of Winona Ryder's character
from the first movie.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:19.169
It has also been reported that Michael Keaton
is returning to reprise his iconic turn as

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:23.650
Beetlejuice himself; he'll be joined here
by returning cast members Ryder and Catherine

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:29.614
O'Hara, with newcomer Monica Bellucci playing
his wife and Justin Theroux playing an unknown character.

00:04:29.614 --> 00:04:34.135
Apparently, Willem Dafoe is also set to play
some sort of afterlife cop.

00:04:34.135 --> 00:04:38.463
While little is known about the plot, we do
know that Burton himself is coming back to direct.

00:04:38.463 --> 00:04:44.030
Beetlejuice 2 is tentatively earmarked for
a September 6th, 2024 release date, but production

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:49.240
delays caused by the SAG-AFTRA strike could
feasibly push the movie down the line.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.129
Roger Ebert once hailed This Is Spinal Tap
as "one of the funniest movies ever made"

00:04:54.129 --> 00:04:56.180
— and it's difficult to disagree with him.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.990
The 1984 mockumentary tells the story of fading
band Spinal Tap, desperately searching for

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.979
musical glory in a world that has forgotten
them.

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:07.820
As they embark on a tour across the United
States, they're filmed by the not-so-talented

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:11.977
documentarian Marty — played by the film's
actual director, Rob Reiner.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:16.900
With its so-terrible-they're-amazing songs
and countless improvised jokes, it's no wonder

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.380
that This Is Spinal Tap became an instant
classic.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.986
And now, Reiner is getting the band back together.

00:05:21.986 --> 00:05:26.100
Original stars Michael McKean, Christopher
Guest, and Harry Shearer will be picking up

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.520
their guitars and rocking 'round Stonehenge
in the film's upcoming sequel, scheduled for

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:35.112
release in 2024 — right in time for the
original's 40th anniversary.

00:05:35.112 --> 00:05:38.753
Here's hoping they can turn this sequel up
to 11.

00:05:38.753 --> 00:05:42.310
We appear to be in the midst of an Eddie Murphy
renaissance.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:46.539
After gradually fading from the spotlight
since his heyday in the '80s and early '90s,

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:48.960
Murphy is suddenly back in a big way.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.840
In the last few years, he gave a critically
acclaimed performance in 2019's Dolemite Is

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:59.000
My Name, made a triumphant return to Saturday
Night Live as host, lined up new standup comedy

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.669
specials for Netflix, and announced a sequel
to one of his biggest hits from the '80s:

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:05.000
Beverly Hills Cop.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.830
"Will you go put your trunks on and get in
this pool?"

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:12.259
Marking the fourth installment in the Beverly
Hills Cop franchise, this newest sequel will

00:06:12.259 --> 00:06:16.419
also be a collaboration between Murphy and
Netflix, after Paramount previously pulled

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:20.419
the plug on a planned Beverly Hills Cop 4
back in 2016.

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:24.789
Murphy will be reprising his role as Axel
Foley, the Detroit cop who repeatedly finds

00:06:24.789 --> 00:06:28.080
himself traveling to Beverly Hills to investigate
various crimes.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.600
Beverly Hills Cop 4 was originally going to
be directed by Bad Boys for Life directors

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:37.821
Adil El Arbi and Bilall Fallah, but after
they dropped out to focus on Batgirl, the

00:06:37.821 --> 00:06:42.889
job went to Mark Molloy, a rising filmmaker
who has gained attention for his Apple commercials.

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:47.591
As for the screenplay, Murphy previously said
he is ready to go as soon as the script is complete.

00:06:47.591 --> 00:06:52.250
And in August 2022, Deadline reported that
Will Beall, best known for story credits on

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.370
Aquaman and Zack Snyder's Justice League,
had joined Axel Foley.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:00.580
This time, Murphy and his fellow Beverly Hills
Cop veterans will be joined by Kevin Bacon,

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:05.150
Joseph Gordon-Levitt, and Zola breakout star
Taylour Paige.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.990
Considering the runaway success of 2018's
Crazy Rich Asians, it would be surprising

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.850
if the film didn't earn a sequel.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:14.366
Well, as it happens, it's actually getting
two.

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:19.210
Based on Kevin Kwan's books of the same names,
China Rich Girlfriend and Rich People Problems

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:23.770
are both moving ahead at Warner Bros., although
it may be a while before we get to see them.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:28.630
Due to the busy schedules of the franchise's
A-list cast and director Jon M. Chu, the next

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:33.270
two installments in the Crazy Rich Asians
saga probably won't be coming anytime soon.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:37.170
It seems like the scripts aren't even completed
yet; Michelle Yeoh told E! News:

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.410
"We are still waiting on it.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.560
We know there's a writer on it, so we'll see."

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.150
That writer, according to Deadline, will be
From Scratch's Amy Wang, who replaces the

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.124
original film's scribes, Peter Chiarelli and
Adele Lim.

00:07:48.124 --> 00:07:53.060
Meanwhile, producer Nina Jacobson says that
the plan is to shoot both sequels back-to-back,

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.340
so that fans aren't waiting years between
the second and third films.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.909
Jacobson admits there'll likely be a wait
for the sequels, but adds:

00:07:59.909 --> 00:08:03.574
"We'll make it up to them on the back end
by shooting two films together."

00:08:03.574 --> 00:08:11.322
"If you can dodge a wrench, you can dodge
a ball."

00:08:11.322 --> 00:08:12.322
"What?"

00:08:12.322 --> 00:08:16.690
It's been two decades since the so-called
"Frat Pack" dominated Hollywood comedy.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:20.599
Ben Stiller and Vince Vaughn, stalwarts of
that scene, collaborated on many mid-2000s

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:26.180
movies, perhaps most notable of which was
2004's Dodgeball: A True Underdog Story.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.810
A broad and wacky sports movie that simultaneously
satirizes sports movie clichés, Dodgeball

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:35.421
is a tale of good vs. evil set on the dodgeball
court.

00:08:35.421 --> 00:08:40.010
Dodgeball wraps up pretty conclusively, but
since it was a massively profitable hit and

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:44.510
an enduring favorite on cable TV, a sequel
is on the way regardless.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:48.910
In April 2023, Deadline reported that 20th
Century Studios had ordered another round

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:49.910
of Dodgeball.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:54.010
The Binge screenwriter Jordan VanDina will
pen the script, taking over from original

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.100
writer-director Rawson Marshall Thurber.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:00.250
A director for this movie is yet to be announced,
but Vaughn has already agreed to reprise his

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:06.006
role from the first Dodgeball, having successfully
pitched his original idea for the movie to VanDina.

00:09:06.006 --> 00:09:10.190
Freaky Friday follows a mother and daughter
who, after magically switching bodies, come

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:14.980
to understand one another better after literally
spending some time in each other's shoes.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:19.340
It's a formula that is easily replicated,
as evidenced by the multiple versions of the

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:23.830
movie released in 1976, 1995, and 2018.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.820
The 2003 take, which stars Jamie Lee Curtis
as stressed-out mother Tess Coleman and Lindsay

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:35.350
Lohan as wannabe rock star daughter Anna Coleman,
earned $160 million at the box office and

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.970
launched Lohan's post-childhood career.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:43.010
On the awards show circuit for 2022's Everything
Everywhere All at Once Curtis repeatedly mentioned

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.130
that she'd like to play Tess Coleman again,
and suggested that she had already engaged

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.850
in preliminary talks with Disney about a sequel.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:54.820
The movie became official in May 2023, when
Curtis and Lohan announced Freaky Friday 2

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.380
in a New York Times retrospective on the first
film.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:01.450
Short film auteur Elyse Hollander has been
hired to write the screenplay in what will

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.590
be her first feature-length project.

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:09.839
It's been over 20 years since audiences followed
effervescent sorority girl Elle Woods to Harvard

00:10:09.839 --> 00:10:13.239
Law School in the bubblegum comedy Legally
Blonde.

00:10:13.239 --> 00:10:17.019
"Elle Woods…

00:10:17.638 --> 00:10:18.897
Welcome to Harvard."

00:10:19.149 --> 00:10:24.589
She continued to ascend the professional ladder
in 2003's Legally Blonde 2: Red, White &amp; Blonde,

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:26.980
which saw Elle head to Washington, D.C.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.180
Now Elle is back.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:33.019
In addition to starring as Elle, Reese Witherspoon
will also act as a producer this time through

00:10:33.019 --> 00:10:37.269
her Hello Sunshine banner, and she's brought
on Never Have I Ever creator Mindy Kaling

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:40.860
and Brooklyn Nine-Nine's Dan Goor to pen the
screenplay.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:44.360
Also returning for the sequel is Jennifer
Coolidge, who starred in both previous films

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:48.971
as Elle's friend Paulette, a character who
Kaling teased will have a "really juicy" role

00:10:48.971 --> 00:10:49.879
in the film.

00:10:49.879 --> 00:10:53.770
As for the rest of the original cast, we're
still not sure who will be returning, but

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:57.779
we do know that there will be "a lot of new
faces" in Legally Blonde 3 — along with

00:10:57.779 --> 00:10:59.161
a lot more diversity.

00:10:59.161 --> 00:11:00.341
Kaling promises:

00:11:00.341 --> 00:11:04.240
"Reflecting the world as it is now is something
that's really important to Reese, and so having

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.010
there be [...] diversity is super, super important.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.760
You can definitely count on that."

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:12.920
We've yet to hear much in the way of plot
details, but as a big fan of the original

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:17.638
films, Kaling is very much looking forward
to revisiting an older and wise Elle Woods.

00:11:17.638 --> 00:11:18.501
She says:

00:11:18.501 --> 00:11:21.710
"I can't wait to see what [...] people will
think of the way we wrote Elle Woods at 40.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:27.260
How Elle Woods is at 40 versus how she was
at 21 has been really fun to imagine."

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:31.490
In an act of divine providence — or maybe
just Hollywood nostalgia — it looks like

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:35.040
Sister Mary Clarence will be donning her habit
once again.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.890
Sister Act 3 will premiere on Disney+ sometime
in the near future.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:43.779
Whoopi Goldberg will indeed be returning as
both star and producer, with Tyler Perry also

00:11:43.779 --> 00:11:48.180
coming on board to produce, Madhuri Shekar
signing on to pen the script, and High School

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:52.300
Musical: The Musical: The Series creator Tim
Federle attached to direct.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:57.920
Released in 1992, the first Sister Act saw
Goldberg play Deloris Van Cartier, a lounge

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.980
singer who goes into witness protection at
a convent after witnessing a murder.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:06.930
Sister Act got a sequel in 1993 with Sister
Act 2: Back in the Habit, which found Deloris

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:11.480
stepping in as a music teacher for a group
of low-achieving students at a Catholic school.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:16.279
Goldberg suggested in her profile for Variety
in 2021 that we could even possibly see some

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:17.414
of those kids again.

00:12:17.414 --> 00:12:18.208
She said:

00:12:18.208 --> 00:12:20.600
"Maybe there's gonna be some of the kids [from
Sister Act 2].

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:21.680
Who can say?"

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:25.630
The rest of the cast is up in the air right
now, but Sister Act 3 is certainly heading

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.015
in the right direction.

00:12:27.015 --> 00:12:30.247
"It has a whole lot of adults to go through.

00:12:30.247 --> 00:12:35.649
So, if they don't get in its way, it could
actually be pretty good."

00:12:35.649 --> 00:12:41.459
Fans of the 1996 bowling comedy Kingpin will
be glad to hear that a sequel is rolling down the pipeline.

00:12:41.459 --> 00:12:45.269
The original film starred Woody Harrelson
as a former bowling prodigy who believes he

00:12:45.269 --> 00:12:50.717
has found his claim to fame when he discovers
an Amish bowling superstar, played by Randy Quaid.

00:12:50.717 --> 00:12:54.260
The movie also starred Bill Murray as Harrelson's
lifelong rival.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:57.980
No details have yet been revealed about the
sequel, other than the fact that Peter and

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:02.399
Bobby Farrelly, who directed the first film,
will be back on board to produce.

00:13:02.399 --> 00:13:06.149
However, it's unclear whether the Farrelly
brothers are intending to write or direct

00:13:06.149 --> 00:13:08.769
the sequel in addition to their producing
duties.

00:13:08.769 --> 00:13:13.110
Similarly, none of the original cast is confirmed
to be returning for the sequel, although fans

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:18.460
would surely welcome another chance to see
Harrelson and Murray unite on the big screen.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.260
Ready for another trip to Genovia?

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:25.570
It certainly looks like Disney is preparing
for a new royal adventure with The Princess Diaries 3.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:29.339
We don't know any plot details yet, and it
doesn't look like anyone has been officially

00:13:29.339 --> 00:13:30.910
cast as of this moment.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.320
However, Anne Hathaway has expressed her desire
for a threequel in the past, so chances are

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:37.839
good she'll be returning to play Mia Thermopolis.

00:13:37.839 --> 00:13:41.410
For her part, it seems like Julie Andrews
plans on sitting this one out, as she told

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.585
The Hollywood Reporter in June 2022:

00:13:43.585 --> 00:13:46.949
"[For] especially me, it's too far down the
line now to go back to it.

00:13:46.949 --> 00:13:51.160
It's a lovely thought, but I don't think it
would probably be possible."

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:55.660
Now one of the most beloved stars to have
ever kicked his way across the silver screen,

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:59.529
Jackie Chan first found Hollywood success
with the action-comedy Rush Hour.

00:13:59.529 --> 00:14:04.930
The 1998 film paired Chan's martial arts-savvy
Hong Kong detective with Chris Tucker's riotous

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:05.655
L.A. cop.

00:14:05.655 --> 00:14:09.649
Together, Chan and Tucker starred in the eighth
highest-grossing movie of the year and kicked

00:14:09.649 --> 00:14:11.667
off two sequels in the process.

00:14:11.667 --> 00:14:13.538
And now a third is on the way.

00:14:13.538 --> 00:14:17.529
At the Red Sea International Film Festival,
Jackie Chan revealed that he's in talks to

00:14:17.529 --> 00:14:18.980
make Rush Hour 4.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:22.970
He added that he was about to go talk with
the director about the upcoming film, although

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:25.090
he didn't reveal the filmmaker's identity.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:29.100
The previous installments in the series were
all helmed by Brett Ratner, but as Ratner

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:34.009
is now persona non grata in Hollywood, a new
director is likely to be stepping up to bat

00:14:34.009 --> 00:14:37.829
— despite Ratner claiming he was making
Rush Hour 4 back in 2018.

00:14:37.829 --> 00:14:41.329
However, it does at least look like Tucker
is coming back.

00:14:41.329 --> 00:14:45.910
Speaking with V-103's Big Tigger Morning Show,
he talked about his upcoming work schedule.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:49.271
"Rush Hour 4, that's something I definitely
will probably drop in there because I love

00:14:49.271 --> 00:14:50.271
working with Jackie."

00:14:50.271 --> 00:14:55.089
No due date yet, but it seems Rush Hour 4
is certainly on the way.

00:14:55.089 --> 00:14:59.840
One of the definitive films of the 1990s,
Election is a pitch-black satire that takes

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:03.730
aim at the U.S. political system through the
lens of a high school election.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:07.820
The movie finds Reese Witherspoon's Tracy
Flick tirelessly campaigning to become student

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.670
body president — and doing whatever it takes
to win.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:15.209
All the while, bitter teacher Jim McAllister
is desperately trying to destroy Tracy's chances

00:15:15.209 --> 00:15:16.699
of earning any votes.

00:15:16.699 --> 00:15:20.990
Now, all these years later, it looks like
Tracy Flick is coming back, determined as

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.769
ever to be #1.

00:15:22.769 --> 00:15:27.634
Tracy Flick Can't Win will reunite Witherspoon
with Alexander Payne, the original movie's director.

00:15:27.634 --> 00:15:32.079
The project is based on the novel by Tom Perrotta,
which finds Flick back at high school, trying

00:15:32.079 --> 00:15:36.600
to become principal while struggling with
a life that hasn't panned out how she planned.

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:40.380
While we don't have a release date yet, expect
the Election sequel to campaign its way to

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:43.509
Paramount+ sometime in the future.

00:15:43.509 --> 00:15:48.709
Hocus Pocus was only a moderate hit during
its initial theatrical release in 1993.

00:15:48.709 --> 00:15:55.000
A Halloween movie released in July for some
reason, it earned around $45 million at the box office.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:00.060
But it became a hit on home video and through
repeated, heavily-watched annual TV broadcasts.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:05.580
By the early 2000s, Hocus Pocus had become
required October viewing for countless viewers.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:10.579
It tells the story of teenager Max, who, along
with his little sister Dani and crush Allison,

00:16:10.579 --> 00:16:13.970
attempt to prevent the return of a trio of
evil witches.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:19.240
Debuting in September 2022, Hocus Pocus 2
set a viewership record for Disney+, racking

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:24.440
up 2.73 billion minutes of watch time over
its first three days of availability.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:30.350
And now a third Hocus Pocus is flying over
to Disney+ too: In June 2023, Disney executive

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:34.330
Sean Bailey told the New York Times that a
third entry in the comedic witch series was

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.806
in the works.

